{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden fixture for computeGoalProgress, shared between app/src/goals/goalProgress.ts",
    "and website/js/goals.js -- two independent implementations of the same",
    "window/progress math (see each file's own header for why they can't import",
    "one another). Lives under tests/fixtures/ (not app/src/goals/ or website/js/)",
    "because it's read by BOTH suites and neither owns the other's directory.",
    "",
    "Every `expected` array was produced by RUNNING the real website/js/goals.js",
    "computeGoalProgress (the two implementations are formula-identical), then",
    "verified by hand against the window/topic/met semantics documented in",
    "goalProgress.ts's own comments -- not just checked for agreement between the",
    "two sides.",
    "",
    "TIMEZONE REPRESENTATION -- read this before touching any timestamp below.",
    "`now` and `startedAt` are LOCAL-TIME-relative: the window math anchors to",
    "LOCAL midnight/week-start/month-start, computed via `new Date(y, mo, d, ...)`",
    "in whatever timezone the test happens to run in. A raw epoch-ms literal",
    "bakes in ONE specific timezone's interpretation of that instant, so a",
    "session meant to sit 1ms before a local-midnight boundary in Pacific can",
    "silently sit 1ms AFTER that boundary in Eastern (or vice versa) -- same",
    "epoch number, different window membership, a fixture that's permanently",
    "wrong outside one timezone. This bit monthly_window_year_rollover_december",
    "for real: both implementations agreed with each other and STILL failed the",
    "fixture on an Eastern machine, because the fixture's own literals were",
    "wrong, not the math.",
    "",
    "So: every `now`/`startedAt` here is given as `nowLocal`/`startedAtLocal`,",
    "a `[year, monthIndex, day, hour, minute, second, ms]` tuple (monthIndex is",
    "0-based, same as `Date`'s constructor -- both readers do",
    "`new Date(y, mo, d, h, mi, s, ms).getTime()`, in THEIR OWN runtime",
    "timezone, not a hardcoded one). Because both nowLocal and startedAtLocal",
    "go through the identical conversion in the identical process, their",
    "relative position (which side of a window boundary a session falls on)",
    "is preserved in ANY timezone, even though the resulting epoch ms differs",
    "from machine to machine. Every case uses *Local parts, including sessions",
    "whose startedAt is simply \"the same instant as now\" -- verified live: on a",
    "UTC+5:30/UTC+13 process those sessions stopped landing on nowMs's calendar",
    "day when only nowMs (not the session) was converted, so this is not",
    "theoretical. DO NOT reintroduce a raw epoch-ms literal for any timestamp",
    "here (window boundaries, day-of-week, or \"now\" itself) -- always use the",
    "*Local parts form; both readers still accept a plain `nowMs`/`startedAt`",
    "number for backward compatibility, but nothing in this file should use it.",
    "",
    "If you change the window/progress math on EITHER side, this fixture stops",
    "being a safe oracle -- regenerate it (see goalProgress.golden.test.ts's",
    "header for the regeneration recipe) and re-verify by inspection, don't just",
    "silence the failing assertions.",
    "",
    "A goal with targetS <= 0 IS covered (nonpositive_target_guards_the_divide).",
    "It used to be excluded, because the two sides disagreed: goalProgress.ts",
    "guarded the divide and returned 0, while website/js/goals.js divided bare",
    "and produced NaN/Infinity. The website now carries the same guard, so the",
    "case is asserted rather than merely documented. It is unreachable through",
    "createGoal/updateGoal or sanitizeRemoteGoals, which both enforce",
    "targetS >= MIN_TARGET_S -- but it is the shape a corrupted or hand-built",
    "synced goal takes, which is why the app guarded it in the first place.",
    "",
    "`labels`/`excludedTopicKeys` (both optional per-case, defaulting to `[]` on",
    "both readers when absent) exercise computeGoalProgress's exclusion filter",
    "(app/src/stats/customLabels.ts's sessionCountsTowardTotals, threaded through",
    "goalProgress.ts's own `labels`/`excludedTopicKeys` params) -- every case",
    "above this comment predates that filter and leaves both unset, which is",
    "exactly why the website's own missing implementation of it went uncaught",
    "here for as long as it did. The four cases below close that blind spot:",
    "a custom label with excludeFromTotals true, an excluded built-in topic",
    "key, an untagged session (must still count despite unrelated exclusions",
    "being active), and an excluded label alongside a non-excluded one in the",
    "same case. Expected values were derived by hand from",
    "stats/customLabels.ts's sessionCountsTowardTotals doc comment, then",
    "confirmed to match both implementations."
  ],
